Scene geometry is authored for this task under the repository's Apache-2.0 license.
No commercial warehouse pack or private research-lab environment is redistributed.

Photo textures: Poly Haven, CC0-1.0 (https://polyhaven.com/license).
The pinned URLs and SHA-256 hashes are in environment/visual_assets.json:
https://polyhaven.com/a/concrete_floor_02
https://polyhaven.com/a/asphalt_02
https://polyhaven.com/a/brick_wall_001
https://polyhaven.com/a/rusty_metal_02
https://polyhaven.com/a/utility_box_01
https://polyhaven.com/a/portable_generator
https://polyhaven.com/a/concrete_road_barrier
Powered by Poly Haven. Discovery uses its public API only at authoring time;
container builds use pinned URLs and SHA-256 hashes. Mesh/texture conversion is
reproducible with environment/fetch_visual_assets.py and its pinned dependencies.

The cameras' render bundle (environment/assets.sha256: 18 maps and ibl.ktx, fetched from the
benchmark's asset dataset at a pinned commit) is drawn by MuJoCo 3.16.0's Filament renderer:
- wall, floor-tile and ceiling maps: from the Unity Asset Store pack "Chernobyl", which the
  benchmark's maintainer holds and supplied for the benchmark; resized to 512 px, the walls'
  dado band desaturated, per-map gains from a fit against path-traced stills of the task's look;
- concrete, timber, rubber and wear maps: from Poly Haven scans, CC0-1.0
  (concrete_floor_worn_001, concrete_wall_008, rough_wood, rusty_metal_02, rubber_tiles);
- six worn floor-paint maps and the window picture: made for this task;
- look.tar, the models that stand in a site (one OBJ set and its pictures at 256 px per model):
  furniture, posters and wall cabinets, the yard's fence, vehicles and plants from the "Chernobyl" pack;
  warehouse stock from the Unity Asset Store packs "Warehouse" and "Factory props"; the airframe from
  "Realistic Drones"; the casualty from the Microsoft Rocketbox avatar library (MIT) in a pose taken from
  one frame of the "Ultimate Animation Collection"; cars from "Realistic Car HD 02". The maintainer holds
  the packs and supplied them for the benchmark; meshes are thinned and re-exported, not the packs' files.
  The litter, the receiver's frame, the blanket and the paper are made for this task;
- ibl.ktx: the image light, a two-tone profile over the elevation made for this task and
  prefiltered with Filament's cmgen (Apache-2.0). No probe of a commercial environment is in it.

Nominal robot visual meshes: Google DeepMind MuJoCo Menagerie at
f3b6013629c7b94f8ee93fd977b161fa8350f9bc.
Crazyflie and Unitree Go1 original license texts accompany this file.
These are simplified benchmark dynamics, not manufacturer-certified digital twins.
